# Prebuilt Bootlin toolchain: x86-64, glibc, stable 2024.05-1.
#
# gcc 13.3.0, glibc 2.39, kernel headers 4.19.315, binutils 2.41.
# The lab boots a kernel built outside Buildroot and only needs a working
# userspace, so building the cross toolchain from source is wasted work: it
# accounts for roughly twelve of the twenty-three minutes of a cold build.
#
# The profile is pinned twice: by VERSION.lock (BUILDROOT_REF selects which
# Buildroot tree describes the profile) and by the sha256 recorded in
# sources/buildroot/toolchain/toolchain-external/toolchain-external-bootlin,
# which BR2_DOWNLOAD_FORCE_CHECK_HASHES verifies on download.
#
# The pinned profile ships kernel headers 4.19, so packages requiring newer
# headers cannot be enabled while this fragment is in use. See the README
# section on the Buildroot toolchain before adding such a package.
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_BOOTLIN=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_BOOTLIN_X86_64_GLIBC_STABLE=y
# BR2_TOOLCHAIN_BUILDROOT is not set
